    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nFor Sale by DNG Online Auction TO REGISTER FOR OUR ONLINE AUCTION on the 30th September 2026 at 12pm.Visit www.dngauctions.ieChoose/ Search for your property of interest, click log in & register to bid and follow the necessary steps.Bidder security required prior to auction date in order to successfully bid on the day.\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to offer sale this traditional detached residence standing on approximately 1.276 acres in the highly popular residential townland of Bohoona, just 1.4 km from the heart of Spiddal Village. Occupying an elevated position within mature grounds, this south facing property enjoys an enviable setting where the peace of the Connemara countryside meets the beauty of Galway's spectacular coastline.Situated along the gateway to Connemara and the Wild Atlantic Way, the location is one of the property's greatest assets. Within minutes are the sandy beaches and shoreline of Spiddal, the renowned Ceardlann Craft Village, local cafés, restaurants, schools and sporting amenities, while Galway City is approximately 19 km away. The R336 coastal route, stretching west through Furbo, Spiddal and into the heart of Connemara, is regarded as one of Ireland's most scenic drives, placing an unrivalled landscape of coastline, mountains and open countryside quite literally on your doorstep.Originally constructed during the 1960s, the residence extends to approximately 67.77sq.m (730 sq.ft) offers spacious accommodation with excellent potential for refurbishment and modernisation. Full of character and authenticity, the property provides purchasers with the opportunity to create a superb family home while retaining the charm of a traditional Connemara residence.Standing on approximately 1.276 acres, the property is complemented by mature gardens, traditional stone boundaries and three useful outbuildings, providing excellent versatility for storage, workshops or hobby farming. The generous site offers both privacy and space, a combination that is becoming increasingly difficult to find so close to Spiddal Village and Galway Bay.Spiddal continues to be one of the West of Ireland's most sought-after coastal villages, celebrated for its vibrant community, Irish-speaking heritage and exceptional quality of life. Whether enjoying a walk along the shoreline, meeting friends in one of the village cafés, exploring Connemara National Park or simply taking in the changing colours across Galway Bay, it is easy to understand why so many people choose to make this part of County Galway their home.\n\nPlease note this property will be offered by online auction (unless sold prior). Vendors may decide to accept pre-auction bids so please register your interest with us to avoid disappointment. The successful bidder is required to pay the balance of 10% deposit and contracts are signed immediately on acceptance of a bid.Properties on generous sites in locations such as this rarely come to the market. Combining an established residence, useful outbuildings and an outstanding coastal setting, this property presents an exciting opportunity for purchasers to restore, modernise and create a home that can be enjoyed for generations to come."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \n\n\nKitchen - \nTraditional entrance hallway providing access to the principal accommodation. Located to the rear of the property with kitchen area fitted units and direct access to the rear yard and gardens.\n\nBathroom - \nComprising bath, wash hand basin and WC.\n\nLiving Room - \nBright and welcoming reception room positioned at the heart of the home, featuring an open fireplace with back boiler and views over the front gardens.\n\nBedroom 1 - \n\n\nBedroom 2 - \n\n\nBedroom 3 - \n\n\nBedroom 4 - \n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> For Sale by DNG Online Auction</li><li> Traditional detached Connemara cottage</li><li> Standing on a fine c. 1.276-acre site</li><li> Accommodation extending to c. 67.77 sq.m (730 sq.ft.)</li><li> Oil-fired central heating</li><li> Elevated setting with mature grounds and stone boundaries</li><li> Three detached outbuildings with excellent potential</li><li> Exceptional renovation opportunity in a sought-after location</li><li> Just 1.4km from the heart of Spiddal Village</li><li> Gateway to Connemara, the Wild Atlantic Way and Galway Bay</ul>"
      },
